Dialogue: 10,0:00:05.54,0:00:11.50,Narrator,,0,0,0,,Long, long ago... deep in\N the mountains beyond mountains...
Dialogue: 10,0:00:11.50,0:00:14.95,Narrator,,0,0,0,,there was a tiny, poor village. {lit: mountains of mountains of mountains - meaning "the absolute boondocks, literal middle of nowhere"}
Dialogue: 10,0:00:14.95,0:00:20.45,Narrator,,0,0,0,,Surrounded by towering peaks, \Nit was like the bottom of a bowl.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:21.24,0:00:27.06,Narrator,,0,0,0,,One year, at the end of winter, \Non the day before New Year's, our story began.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:28.03,0:00:30.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Our house is just up ahead. {just gonna put a disclaimer in here that the audio in this source is atrocious}
Dialogue: 10,0:00:30.53,0:00:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry to trouble you.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:32.43,0:00:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't you cold, traveler?
Dialogue: 10,0:00:34.97,0:00:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I am not cold.
Dialogue: 10,0:00:47.71,0:00:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandma, I've come home! {baa-sama = grandma - so his wife I assume}
Dialogue: 10,0:00:51.57,0:00:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandma!
Dialogue: 10,0:00:53.29,0:00:54.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh? {hai?}
Dialogue: 10,0:00:58.13,0:01:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now, you're back already?
Dialogue: 10,0:01:02.16,0:01:04.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, is this a traveler?
Dialogue: 10,0:01:04.62,0:01:06.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, hello there.
Dialogue: 10,0:01:06.70,0:01:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Seems nobody else would\N let him stay the night.
Dialogue: 10,0:01:10.54,0:01:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,This man was sitting out there in the snow.
Dialogue: 10,0:01:13.59,0:01:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, dear me!
Dialogue: 10,0:01:15.38,0:01:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then, come in, please. Quick!
Dialogue: 10,0:01:23.08,0:01:25.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow's New Year's Day,
Dialogue: 10,0:01:25.42,0:01:27.86,Default,,0,0,0,,and we've got nothing at all to offer... {meaning [to treat you, a guest, with]}
Dialogue: 10,0:01:26.75,0:01:28.37,Overlap,,0,0,0,,Oh no, don't mind her!
Dialogue: 10,0:01:28.37,0:01:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, please at least have some pickles \Nand spend the New Year with us.
Dialogue: 10,0:01:33.59,0:01:38.32,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. Even if we don't have much, \Nwe still have to welcome the New Year's Spirit. {oshogatsu-san = new-year-san - this grandpa's actual name}
Dialogue: 10,0:01:48.68,0:01:49.98,Default,,0,0,0,,This is good.
Dialogue: 10,0:01:52.40,0:01:59.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, right! I'm an old fool, I almost forgot! \NI've got something for you as well. There!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:01.98,0:02:04.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! Are those mochi?
Dialogue: 10,0:02:04.48,0:02:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Such beautiful white cakes... {from expensive white rice as opposed to simple grey one that the poor always ate}
Dialogue: 10,0:02:06.64,0:02:09.60,Default,,0,0,0,,And one more thing! Let's see...
Dialogue: 10,0:02:09.60,0:02:10.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Here!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:11.57,0:02:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Some sake for you!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:12.90,0:02:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodness!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:14.70,0:02:18.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's have ourselves\N a merry New Year's Eve together.
Dialogue: 10,0:02:18.47,0:02:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, isn't that wonderful!
Dialogue: 10,0:02:21.36,0:02:23.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Feels like we're dreaming.
Dialogue: 10,0:02:23.56,0:02:29.62,Narrator,,0,0,0,,That night unexpectedly turned \Ninto a truly joyful New Year's Eve.
Dialogue: 10,0:02:24.24,0:02:31.82,Song,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow is New Year's Day\NNew Year's is a wonderful thing! {shougatsu ha ii mon da - traditional japanese new year's song for singing together or while playing badminton or other NY-associated activities; it's just 5 lines on repeat: お正月はいいもんだ〜\N     雪より白い餅食って\N     油のような酒飲んで\N     明日は明日はお正月\N     お正月はいいもんだ〜 ♪}
Dialogue: 10,0:02:31.82,0:02:41.50,Song,,0,0,0,,Eating mochi whiter than snow\Nand drinking sake smooth as oil
Dialogue: 10,0:02:41.50,0:02:45.97,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing
Dialogue: 10,0:02:45.97,0:02:48.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Great, great! {??}
Dialogue: 10,0:02:48.02,0:02:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, good! Good, good...
Dialogue: 10,0:02:52.81,0:02:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Dancing like this even\N straightens out your back.
Dialogue: 10,0:02:56.86,0:03:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, we've had \Nsuch a happy New Year's Eve.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:01.78,0:03:05.80,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my first time ever having \Nsuch a happy New Year's Eve too.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:05.80,0:03:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Seriously.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:07.49,0:03:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,If only there were children here too, \Nit'd truly be a happy New Year.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:11.78,0:03:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,There you go again.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:13.46,0:03:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandma's started her favorite complaint again.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:16.25,0:03:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You're right...
Dialogue: 10,0:03:18.30,0:03:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It just happened. {without thinking}
Dialogue: 10,0:03:21.15,0:03:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Saying it now won't change a thing.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:23.94,0:03:27.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We were never blessed with children.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:27.79,0:03:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What? You two want children?
Dialogue: 10,0:03:31.70,0:03:33.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:33.41,0:03:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I shall grant your wish.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:39.00,0:03:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,At daybreak, go to the foot\N of Doudou Mountain. {ドードー - proper name, though usually doudou means "bold/straightforward", dunno if that has anything to do with it}
Dialogue: 10,0:03:42.08,0:03:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a beech forest there.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:45.76,0:03:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Go to the spring within it.
Dialogue: 10,0:03:49.23,0:03:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well then, farewell!
Dialogue: 10,0:03:58.01,0:04:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandma, ain't this a yuzuriha leaf? {false daphne (Daphniphyllum macropodum); yuzuriha​}
Dialogue: 10,0:04:01.58,0:04:07.31,Default,,0,0,0,,A yuzuriha? The one they say\N the New Year's Spirit rides on? {Nursery rhymes about the descent of the New Year's god (Shogatsu-sama) riding on a yuzuriha tree can be found throughout Japan. [21] The reason why the yuzuriha became the vehicle of the New Year's god is that, just as ancestral spirits pass on their legacy to new life, when the new leaves of the yuzuriha tree sprout in spring, the old leaves fall as if to pass on the legacy. Later generations believed that the ancestral spirits ascended to the heavens riding on these fallen leaves.}
Dialogue: 10,0:04:07.31,0:04:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep. {\i1}That{\i0} yuzuriha!
Dialogue: 10,0:04:21.06,0:04:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandma! Hurry! Grandma!
Dialogue: 10,0:04:33.17,0:04:34.44,Default,,0,0,0,,A baby!
Dialogue: 10,0:04:35.11,0:04:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,A baby! It's a baby!
Dialogue: 10,0:04:39.01,0:04:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now... Goodness gracious!
Dialogue: 10,0:04:44.74,0:04:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,There, there. What a good child. \NSuch a good child...
Dialogue: 10,0:04:50.02,0:04:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh? Another yuzuriha leaf.
Dialogue: 10,0:04:53.00,0:04:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,So then, that white-haired old man was...
Dialogue: 10,0:04:56.54,0:05:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. He really {\i1}was{\i0}\N the New Year's Spirit!
Dialogue: 10,0:05:05.44,0:05:13.18,Song,,0,0,0,,Shanshaka, shanshaka\NByu-byu, byu-byuun {miraculously, this has full lyrics on the web: https://animesongz.com/lyric/7283/27707 ; しゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\N\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん\Nしゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\N\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん\Nキラキラ しゃきしゃき\Nまえがみ太郎は\N\Nどうどの森の\N生まれだぞい\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\N太郎の白馬はつばめとび\Nホレ かけのぼれ\Nかけぬけろ\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\Nどうどのまものは\N火の鳥じゃ\Nソラ 空に舞え 空に舞え\N\N僕 僕 風ふかん村の\Nまえがみ太郎さ\N\N天 ゆるがす\Nいなずまさえも\N\N地 ひきさく\N大雨さえも\N\Nへいちゃら\Nへいちゃら\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\N太郎のつるぎで お姫様\Nソレ 助け出せ 助け出せ\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\N御殿の大蛇は悪者じゃ\Nヤァー きりかかれ\Nきりかかれ\N\N僕 僕 風ふかん村の\Nまえがみ太郎さ\N\N天 ゆるがす\Nいなずまさえも\N\N地 ひきさく\N大雨さえも\N\Nへいちゃら\Nへいちゃら\N\N僕 僕 風ふかん村の\Nまえがみ太郎さ\N\N天 ゆるがす\Nいなずまさえも\N\N地 ひきさく\N大雨さえも\N\Nへいちゃら\Nへいちゃら\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん}
Dialogue: 10,0:05:13.18,0:05:16.70,Song,,0,0,0,,The monster of Doudou Mountain is the Firebird
Dialogue: 10,0:05:16.70,0:05:24.86,Song,,0,0,0,,Fly, fly across the sky! Fly, fly across the sky! {/phoenix}
Dialogue: 10,0:05:24.86,0:05:32.53,Song,,0,0,0,,Me, me, from Kazefukan Village\NI'm Maegami Tarou {kaze = wind, fuku = to blow, -n = not; so together I think it means "the village where the wind doesn't blow"; there's no village like that irl or in any other fairy tale}
Dialogue: 10,0:05:32.53,0:05:36.45,Song,,0,0,0,,Even thunder that shakes the heavens
Dialogue: 10,0:05:36.45,0:05:40.07,Song,,0,0,0,,Even pouring rain that tears the earth apart
Dialogue: 10,0:05:40.47,0:05:45.78,Song,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,2000)}Doesn't scare me! {へいちゃら =unconcerned (about); unbothered}
Dialogue: 10,0:05:45.78,0:05:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, there he goes, riding that horse again.
Dialogue: 10,0:05:49.02,0:05:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah! W-Watch out!
Dialogue: 10,0:05:51.55,0:05:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, mister! {-tachi }
Dialogue: 10,0:05:52.39,0:05:53.47,Overlap,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 10,0:05:53.47,0:05:55.41,Overlap,,0,0,0,,You ain't supposed\N to ride horses around here!
Dialogue: 10,0:05:56.16,0:05:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,That Maegami Tarou...
Dialogue: 10,0:05:58.26,0:06:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a rule in this village that horses \Nain't supposed to gallop through it.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:02.31,0:06:07.37,Narrator,,0,0,0,,The baby given by the New Year's Spirit \Nwas named Tarou.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:07.87,0:06:10.56,Narrator,,0,0,0,,Ever since he was little,\N he loved horses dearly,
Dialogue: 10,0:06:10.56,0:06:14.36,Narrator,,0,0,0,,and by the age of seven or eight,\Nhe was already riding on Kuro's back,
Dialogue: 10,0:06:14.36,0:06:18.81,Narrator,,0,0,0,,trotting along narrow mountain paths\N no one else dared to use. {kuro = black}
Dialogue: 10,0:06:18.81,0:06:20.92,Narrator,,0,0,0,,The villagers were amazed, saying,
Dialogue: 10,0:06:20.92,0:06:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That boy's something special, \Nat so young an age! {maegami no torenu = before his forelock is taken - idk what he means, but basically "maegami" also means "A boy with bangs. A boy who has not yet come of age."; don't think there's any way to draw a connection between forelock and young age in English?}
Dialogue: 10,0:06:24.69,0:06:29.67,Narrator,,0,0,0,,And so, before long, \Neveryone began calling him Maegami Tarou.
Dialogue: 10,0:06:49.38,0:06:51.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Doudou Mountain's rumbling again! {where the firebird lives}
Dialogue: 10,0:07:09.45,0:07:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Please! Kuro, get up! \NCome on, get up already!
Dialogue: 10,0:07:12.90,0:07:15.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Sheesh, you're so helpless. \NYour legs gave out on you. {from fear maybe?}
Dialogue: 10,0:07:18.74,0:07:19.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, stand up!
Dialogue: 10,0:07:19.74,0:07:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou! Tarou! Where are you, Tarou?
Dialogue: 10,0:07:22.81,0:07:24.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, I'm over here!
Dialogue: 10,0:07:25.65,0:07:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, dear me... Can't you hear Doudou Mountain roaring?
Dialogue: 10,0:07:29.29,0:07:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,We need to hide, quick!
Dialogue: 10,0:07:30.40,0:07:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to, but Kuro here...
Dialogue: 10,0:07:35.19,0:07:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou, what's happened here?
Dialogue: 10,0:07:37.59,0:07:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever Doudou Mountain starts rumbling, \NKuro's legs give out on him.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:41.75,0:07:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,See there? I told you not to ride him. \NYou've angered Doudou Mountain's spirit.
Dialogue: 10,0:07:49.59,0:07:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,There it goes again! \NHurry up and get outta there, Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:07:53.01,0:07:56.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave that helpless horse. Hurry!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:01.32,0:08:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,But Grandpa, Doudou Mountain sure is beautiful.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:04.28,0:08:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I'd like to go there someday.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:06.39,0:08:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, what're you saying?! \NMonsters live there!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:10.22,0:08:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:12.78,0:08:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah! It's dangerous! Come on, Kuro! Move it!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:22.44,0:08:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Kuro! Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:24.57,0:08:29.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Kuro! Kuro, where are you going?! Wait!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:34.58,0:08:36.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou, boy...
Dialogue: 10,0:08:36.45,0:08:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, no more riding Kuro\N all over the place.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:42.59,0:08:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Grandma.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:44.19,0:08:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't ride Kuro again until I go see the monster on Doudou Mountain.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:47.73,0:08:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you saying, Tarou?!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:49.80,0:08:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't go thinking such terrifying things!
Dialogue: 10,0:08:53.33,0:08:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Truth is, I'd kinda like to see the monster on Doudou Mountain myself one day.
Dialogue: 10,0:08:58.62,0:09:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh dear, now even Grandpa's saying it.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:01.54,0:09:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, they've said since long ago \Nthat a golden bird lives on that mountain.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:07.15,0:09:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,A golden bird?
Dialogue: 10,0:09:08.43,0:09:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:09.67,0:09:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,They say that if the bird ever takes flight, \Nthis village will be blessed with happiness.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:14.52,0:09:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We don't rightly know\N what that means, though.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:21.30,0:09:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,A golden bird, huh...
Dialogue: 10,0:09:47.99,0:09:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, will you be okay \Ncarrying all that yourself?
Dialogue: 10,0:09:51.16,0:09:53.56,Default,,0,0,0,,You still can't beat me yet.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:54.75,0:09:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Careful, Tarou. One wrong step \Nand you'll tumble straight into the river gorge.
Dialogue: 10,0:09:59.60,0:10:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I've ridden Kuro down this path before, you know.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:02.34,0:10:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That's true. You really did listen\N to us in the end. {about not riding kuro ever again}
Dialogue: 10,0:10:06.17,0:10:08.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You've not ridden him once\N since then, have you?
Dialogue: 10,0:10:12.31,0:10:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, tomorrow's New Year's Day.
Dialogue: 10,0:10:15.08,0:10:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Ah, tomorrow's New Year's, yeah. \NLet's hurry home and make millet cakes. {awamochi = millet dough cake; millet mochi}
Dialogue: 10,0:10:21.62,0:10:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandma must be getting\N restless waiting for us. {with her neck stretched out - meaning "impatient"}
Dialogue: 10,0:10:24.89,0:10:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:31.29,0:11:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Kuro, we've wandered onto Doudou Mountain.
Dialogue: 10,0:11:44.87,0:11:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Kuro, what's wrong? \NDid you notice something? Hey, Kuro!
Dialogue: 10,0:11:52.85,0:11:54.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Watch out!
Dialogue: 10,0:11:54.87,0:11:56.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Stand still, Kuro!
Dialogue: 10,0:12:15.14,0:12:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,The monster's nearby, isn't it?
Dialogue: 10,0:12:18.01,0:12:19.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Kuro!
Dialogue: 10,0:12:21.61,0:12:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Hup!
Dialogue: 10,0:12:30.92,0:12:35.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What now? Your legs gave out again?\NYou're such a coward.
Dialogue: 10,0:12:35.94,0:12:39.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine, I'll go alone. \NYou stay here and wait.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:05.84,0:13:09.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure is pitch black in there... and hot too.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:25.54,0:13:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Monster of Doudou Mountain, \Nare you here?! {mamono}
Dialogue: 10,0:13:34.78,0:13:36.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 10,0:13:40.22,0:13:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 10,0:13:41.99,0:13:45.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not a monster. {mamono - has negative connotations of "Devil/evil spirit"}
Dialogue: 10,0:13:45.32,0:13:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I am Firebird! {[and not some monster]}{/phoenix}{gonna assume that's his proper name and not the name of the kind of bird}
Dialogue: 10,0:13:47.83,0:13:49.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Firebird?
Dialogue: 10,0:13:49.53,0:13:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, Firebird.
Dialogue: 10,0:13:57.54,0:14:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Firebird! Because of your howling,\N our village's in trouble! {omae no okage de ora no mura ga komatteru zo}
Dialogue: 10,0:14:03.48,0:14:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,What was that?
Dialogue: 10,0:14:04.93,0:14:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Because of your howling,\N Doudou Mountain goes wild.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:08.58,0:14:10.87,Default,,0,0,0,,It starts spouting hot rocks everywhere,
Dialogue: 10,0:14:10.87,0:14:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,and it messes up the farmers' fields!
Dialogue: 10,0:14:13.15,0:14:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:14.42,0:14:15.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Then stop howling!
Dialogue: 10,0:14:15.86,0:14:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not howling because I want to. {/like it}
Dialogue: 10,0:14:18.59,0:14:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,For reasons unknown, my body has\N grown weak, and I can no longer fly.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:24.33,0:14:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The pain of it makes me thrash and cry out.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:28.90,0:14:30.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to hear that.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:30.80,0:14:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The Firebird cannot die.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:32.64,0:14:34.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I only know how to live.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:34.98,0:14:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,But if I cannot fly, \Nthen living itself is unbearable.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:39.42,0:14:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What am I to do?
Dialogue: 10,0:14:45.89,0:14:48.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if you ask me that, I wouldn't know. {lit: if you ask me such things, it's a problem}
Dialogue: 10,0:14:50.26,0:14:56.18,Default,,0,0,0,,In this wide world, there may be someone\N who knows what should be done.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:56.96,0:14:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, little one.
Dialogue: 10,0:14:58.08,0:15:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Maegami Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:00.03,0:15:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. Tarou, go ask in my place. Please.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:06.94,0:15:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I want to soar through\N the skies once more!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:15.70,0:15:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I got it. I'll travel this wide world\N and find out how to make you fly again.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:23.46,0:15:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll definitely make it\N so you can fly again! Sit tight!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:28.13,0:15:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you, Maegami Tarou.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:37.20,0:15:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:39.19,0:15:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's daybreak!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:43.21,0:15:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Right... It's New Year's Day.
Dialogue: 10,0:15:48.02,0:15:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 10,0:15:50.58,0:15:55.36,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the New Year!  It's the New Year!{oshougatsu da?}
Dialogue: 10,0:15:55.36,0:15:59.69,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm setting out into \Nthe wide world starting today!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:04.23,0:16:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now, Maegami Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:07.96,0:16:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Been a while.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:10.44,0:16:12.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Who might you be, mister? {grandpa}
Dialogue: 10,0:16:13.91,0:16:18.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You say that, even though you just shouted \Nmy name at the top of your lungs!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:18.71,0:16:21.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I did? Your name?
Dialogue: 10,0:16:22.62,0:16:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, you must be the New Year's Spirit! {literally "new year-san"}
Dialogue: 10,0:16:26.65,0:16:30.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you're my guardian spirit! \NI was born on New Year's Day, after all!
Dialogue: 10,0:16:30.42,0:16:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You know me. You know me very well.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:33.21,0:16:38.97,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way, Tarou, it sounded like you \Nwere saying you're heading off somewhere.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:39.67,0:16:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:40.83,0:16:46.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna travel the whole world \Nto find out how the Firebird can fly again.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:47.14,0:16:49.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! As the New Year's Spirit, \Nmaybe you know something?
Dialogue: 10,0:16:49.94,0:16:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I do.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:52.05,0:16:55.85,Default,,0,0,0,,In this world, there is a mysterious treasure \Ncalled the Water of Life.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:55.85,0:16:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,If you sprinkle that water on the Firebird, \Nits strength will return.
Dialogue: 10,0:16:59.99,0:17:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And if the Firebird takes flight from that mountain,
Dialogue: 10,0:17:03.18,0:17:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,happiness will come to your village too.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:06.19,0:17:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,So all I need is the Water of Life?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:07.93,0:17:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,But even then, it still won't be able to fly.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:11.10,0:17:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:12.73,0:17:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,For the Firebird to fly, \Nit must cast something away first.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:17.41,0:17:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless the Firebird realizes that itself, \Nit can never fly again.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:22.64,0:17:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Cast something away?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:24.13,0:17:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:25.51,0:17:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,But for now, all you need to do \Nis bring back the Water of Life.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:29.88,0:17:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Where do I find that water?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:32.22,0:17:35.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Somewhere in this wide world!
Dialogue: 10,0:17:36.12,0:17:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll find it!
Dialogue: 10,0:17:38.83,0:17:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Go on, then.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:42.33,0:17:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, ride this steed.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:44.70,0:17:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll lend you my horse. \NNo need to hold back.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:48.57,0:17:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But mind you, this horse flies through the sky.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:52.21,0:17:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,If you can't master it, you'll be helpless.
Dialogue: 10,0:17:56.14,0:17:57.16,Default,,0,0,0,,A flying horse?
Dialogue: 10,0:17:57.58,0:18:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now? Think you can ride it?
Dialogue: 10,0:18:04.88,0:18:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,All right! I'll give it a try!
Dialogue: 10,0:18:16.78,0:18:24.67,Song,,0,0,0,,{same song as before} Shanshaka, shanshaka\NByu-byu, byu-byuun {キラキラ しゃきしゃき\Nまえがみ太郎は\N\Nどうどの森の\N生まれだぞい\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\N太郎の白馬はつばめとび\Nホレ かけのぼれ\Nかけぬけろ \N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\Nどうどのまものは\N火の鳥じゃ\Nソラ 空に舞え 空に舞え\N\N僕 僕 風ふかん村の\Nまえがみ太郎さ\N\N天 ゆるがす\Nいなずまさえも\N\N地 ひきさく\N大雨さえも\N\Nへいちゃら\Nへいちゃら\N}
Dialogue: 10,0:18:24.67,0:18:28.44,Song,,0,0,0,,Glitter glitter, swishity-swish
Dialogue: 10,0:18:28.44,0:18:37.37,Song,,0,0,0,,Maegami Tarou was born in Doudou Forest
Dialogue: 10,0:18:39.89,0:18:44.03,Song,,0,0,0,,Shanshaka hyun-hyura byu-byuun
Dialogue: 10,0:18:44.03,0:18:47.28,Song,,0,0,0,,Tarou's white horse is Tsubametobi {tsubametobi means "swallow-tailed kite" - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swallow-tailed_kite}
Dialogue: 10,0:18:47.28,0:18:51.76,Song,,0,0,0,,Come on, race uphill
Dialogue: 10,0:18:51.76,0:18:55.44,Song,,0,0,0,,Race on through
Dialogue: 10,0:18:55.44,0:18:59.44,Song,,0,0,0,,Shanshaka hyun-hyura byu-byuun
Dialogue: 10,0:18:59.44,0:19:02.81,Song,,0,0,0,,The monster of Doudou Mountain is the Firebird
Dialogue: 10,0:19:02.81,0:19:07.00,Song,,0,0,0,,Fly, fly across the sky
Dialogue: 10,0:19:07.00,0:19:11.00,Song,,0,0,0,,Fly across the sky!
Dialogue: 10,0:19:11.00,0:19:18.24,Song,,0,0,0,,Me, me, from Kazefukan Village\NI'm Maegami Tarou
Dialogue: 10,0:19:18.59,0:19:22.15,Song,,0,0,0,,Even thunder that shakes the heavens
Dialogue: 10,0:19:22.68,0:19:26.67,Song,,0,0,0,,Even pouring rain that tears the earth apart
Dialogue: 10,0:19:26.67,0:19:31.89,Song,,0,0,0,,Doesn't scare me!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:02.62,0:20:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! He did it! He really did!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:05.96,0:20:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He done did it!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:13.35,0:20:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with you?
Dialogue: 10,0:20:26.70,0:20:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You're really amazing!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:28.93,0:20:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's be friends, white horse!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:32.27,0:20:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Please call me Tsubametobi. It's my name.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:35.87,0:20:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi? That's a fine name.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:38.47,0:20:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Tarou, you're a strong boy indeed, \Nmastering that horse. {he's riding that yuzuriha leaf from before}
Dialogue: 10,0:20:44.82,0:20:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now go, Maegami Tarou.
Dialogue: 10,0:20:47.05,0:20:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Go see the wide world!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:49.75,0:20:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,As for Kuro, leave him to me. \NI'll take him back to your home!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:55.14,0:20:57.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, New Year's Spirit!
Dialogue: 10,0:20:57.22,0:21:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,And goodbye, Kuro! \NGoodbye, New Year's Spirit!
Dialogue: 10,0:21:00.34,0:21:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye! Fare thee well!
Dialogue: 10,0:21:03.31,0:21:04.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Hup!
Dialogue: 10,0:21:20.35,0:21:23.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, I'm hungry. Let's take a rest.
Dialogue: 10,0:21:23.43,0:21:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 10,0:21:24.25,0:21:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, over there looks nice! \NTsubametobi, land by that lake.
Dialogue: 10,0:21:28.12,0:21:30.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's land.
Dialogue: 10,0:21:41.15,0:21:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, I brought some millet mochi. Want some?
Dialogue: 10,0:21:46.41,0:21:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Gladly.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:06.26,0:22:06.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 10,0:22:09.91,0:22:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Wh-What's that? A calf?
Dialogue: 10,0:22:13.03,0:22:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,That's an Ushi-Oni child. {cow-demon: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ushi-oni}
Dialogue: 10,0:22:15.38,0:22:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,An Ushi-Oni?
Dialogue: 10,0:22:34.02,0:22:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,This looks tasty.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:36.36,0:22:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,That's millet mochi. \NYou've never had it before?
Dialogue: 10,0:22:39.60,0:22:41.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Nope. I wanna try some.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:41.96,0:22:43.36,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's mine.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:44.36,0:22:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. Then let's split it in half.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:47.37,0:22:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No, let's split it into three parts.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:49.19,0:22:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,One each for Tsubametobi, me, and you.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:51.64,0:22:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yes! That sounds better!
Dialogue: 10,0:22:55.11,0:22:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Please split it.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:57.21,0:22:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 10,0:22:59.25,0:23:00.28,Default,,0,0,0,,There.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:07.92,0:23:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah...
Dialogue: 10,0:23:09.49,0:23:10.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it good?
Dialogue: 10,0:23:10.43,0:23:11.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It is!
Dialogue: 10,0:23:11.53,0:23:14.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never eaten anything this good before!
Dialogue: 10,0:23:14.66,0:23:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Glad to hear you liked it.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:17.30,0:23:19.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a beautiful horse.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:19.23,0:23:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:38.12,0:23:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You like this steed?
Dialogue: 10,0:23:39.79,0:23:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I like it. I want it!
Dialogue: 10,0:23:41.82,0:23:43.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you give it to me?
Dialogue: 10,0:23:43.72,0:23:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,No way.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:44.93,0:23:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi's my precious friend.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:47.46,0:23:49.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't just hand him over.
Dialogue: 10,0:23:55.50,0:24:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna ride this horse!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:00.34,0:24:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't say such selfish things.
Dialogue: 10,0:24:02.28,0:24:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,No! No! I want it!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:10.48,0:24:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:11.48,0:24:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 10,0:24:13.35,0:24:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's run!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:16.66,0:24:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,No! No! You can't go!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:18.68,0:24:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't care about the horse, \Njust stay and play with me some more!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:22.80,0:24:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,But we've got places to be too.
Dialogue: 10,0:24:26.40,0:24:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,No! No! Please stay and play!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:32.01,0:24:34.41,Default,,0,0,0,,This is bad, Tsubametobi.
Dialogue: 10,0:24:34.41,0:24:40.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Please stay and play! Stay and play!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:44.42,0:24:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, something came out!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:46.55,0:24:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Mom...
Dialogue: 10,0:24:51.26,0:24:53.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the mother Ushi-Oni! Run for it!
Dialogue: 10,0:24:53.23,0:24:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:09.02,0:25:10.91,Default,,0,0,0,,No, stop it!
Dialogue: 10,0:25:18.16,0:25:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, now! Don't go saying\N selfish things like that!
Dialogue: 10,0:25:21.26,0:25:22.92,Default,,0,0,0,,But I... But...
Dialogue: 10,0:25:22.92,0:25:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What? You dare talk back\N to your own mother?
Dialogue: 10,0:25:27.19,0:25:28.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Never.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:28.33,0:25:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Want some milk?
Dialogue: 10,0:25:30.96,0:25:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Want!
Dialogue: 10,0:25:33.10,0:25:34.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, there.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:38.04,0:25:40.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry my kid caused you trouble.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:44.80,0:25:48.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right. He's still little.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:48.70,0:25:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,That's kind of you to say.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:51.92,0:25:54.64,Default,,0,0,0,,So then, where are you headed?
Dialogue: 10,0:25:54.64,0:25:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going out into the wide world \Nto search for the Water of Life.
Dialogue: 10,0:25:57.69,0:26:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam Ushi-Oni Mother, \Nyou wouldn't happen to know where to get some?
Dialogue: 10,0:26:00.89,0:26:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So sorry. I don't know either, \Nbut beyond here, on Nakibiso Mountain, {weirdly specific word but doesn't seem to mean anything}
Dialogue: 10,0:26:06.07,0:26:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,there's a one-eyed, one-legged old mountain spirit who's lived for two thousand years. {yamanji - literally "mountain old man" - dunno what it is exactly, maybe "mountain hermit"}
Dialogue: 10,0:26:10.24,0:26:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe he knows something.
Dialogue: 10,0:26:13.24,0:26:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Nakibiso Mountain it is.\N Off we go!
Dialogue: 10,0:26:16.73,0:26:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a brave child. We've guarded \Nthe waters of this swamp for many years,
Dialogue: 10,0:26:23.72,0:26:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,but people say Ushi-Oni lick \Nthe shadows of humans and kill them, {It is said that there is an ushi-oni at the waterfall basin in Wado River. People who have their shadows licked by one would get a high fever and die in a few days, and to avoid this, one can provide the ushi-oni with its favorite thing, some alcohol, every year at new years.[6]}
Dialogue: 10,0:26:27.96,0:26:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,so nobody's ever ventured this far.
Dialogue: 10,0:26:29.96,0:26:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You must be a very brave kid!
Dialogue: 10,0:26:32.03,0:26:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, out there in the wide world, \Nthere are all sorts of incredible things waiting.
Dialogue: 10,0:26:38.53,0:26:43.55,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right. I've got this Tsubametobi\N the New Year's Spirit lent me. {and that's why he's not afraid to face ushi-oni?}
Dialogue: 10,0:26:43.55,0:26:46.64,Default,,0,0,0,,What? The New Year's Spirit did?!
Dialogue: 10,0:26:46.64,0:26:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. Then as a farewell gift, \NI'll grant you double strength.
Dialogue: 10,0:26:51.50,0:26:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Double strength? \NWhat kind of power's that?
Dialogue: 10,0:26:55.02,0:26:57.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It means you'll have twice \Nthe strength of your opponent.
Dialogue: 10,0:26:57.40,0:26:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,If your enemy is as strong as five men,\N you'll be as strong as ten.
Dialogue: 10,0:26:59.87,0:27:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,If they have the strength of ten men...
Dialogue: 10,0:27:01.79,0:27:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I know! Then I'll have\N the strength of thirty men!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:04.86,0:27:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Tarou, that's wrong. \NTwenty men.
Dialogue: 10,0:27:10.80,0:27:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now, I'll grant you double strength!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:23.04,0:27:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,There, all done.
Dialogue: 10,0:27:24.31,0:27:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,If your enemy has the strength of five men, \Nyou'll have ten. If he has thirty...
Dialogue: 10,0:27:28.02,0:27:30.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I know! Then I'll have\N seventy men's strength!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:30.85,0:27:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou, you're wrong again!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:32.60,0:27:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen carefully. If you're ever in trouble on your journey and need strength, call out my name!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:38.83,0:27:41.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay! Thanks, Ushi-Oni Mother!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:41.41,0:27:43.26,Default,,0,0,0,,See ya!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:43.26,0:27:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Take care!
Dialogue: 10,0:27:47.74,0:27:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, is that Nakibiso Mountain far?
Dialogue: 10,0:27:50.40,0:27:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. We must hurry.
Dialogue: 10,0:27:56.61,0:27:59.95,Narrator,,0,0,0,,And so, Tarou finally met
Dialogue: 10,0:28:00.78,0:28:04.85,Narrator,,0,0,0,,the one-eyed, one-legged mountain spirit.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:10.82,0:28:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The Water of Life?
Dialogue: 10,0:28:12.96,0:28:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. Do you know anything\N about it, One-Eyed Mountain Spirit?
Dialogue: 10,0:28:25.17,0:28:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,All you do is sigh.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:27.84,0:28:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He's remembering things\N from two thousand years ago.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:30.81,0:28:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's give him some more time.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:34.08,0:28:36.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The Water of Life...
Dialogue: 10,0:28:44.11,0:28:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You really don't know?
Dialogue: 10,0:28:47.29,0:28:50.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Nope, haven't got a clue. I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:50.61,0:28:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's quite all right, Mountain Spirit.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:53.20,0:28:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks a lot.
Dialogue: 10,0:28:54.84,0:28:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be on my way, then.
Dialogue: 10,0:29:15.79,0:29:21.69,Narrator,,0,0,0,,Across mountains and valleys, \NTarou continued his long, long journey.
Dialogue: 10,0:29:21.69,0:29:24.55,Narrator,,0,0,0,,But nowhere could he find the Water of Life.
Dialogue: 10,0:29:24.55,0:29:30.57,Narrator,,0,0,0,,Nor did he meet anyone\N who knew where it was.
Dialogue: 10,0:29:53.08,0:29:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou. Wake up, Tarou! Dinner's ready.
Dialogue: 10,0:30:11.11,0:30:12.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, good morning, Tsubametobi.
Dialogue: 10,0:30:12.76,0:30:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you awake now, Tarou?
Dialogue: 10,0:30:14.75,0:30:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:30:15.42,0:30:16.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa! Amazing!
Dialogue: 10,0:30:30.86,0:30:33.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that over there? \NLet's check it out!
Dialogue: 10,0:30:38.09,0:30:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What is that thing?
Dialogue: 10,0:30:39.24,0:30:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a whale.
Dialogue: 10,0:30:40.51,0:30:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,A whale?
Dialogue: 10,0:30:41.54,0:30:44.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. A whale from the sea. {lit: born in the sea}
Dialogue: 10,0:30:45.01,0:30:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But this is strange. \NHow did it end up all the way out here?
Dialogue: 10,0:30:48.55,0:30:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, let's ask him about the Water of Life.
Dialogue: 10,0:30:54.29,0:30:57.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did I ever come all the way out here?
Dialogue: 10,0:30:57.86,0:31:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't move forward, and I can't go back.
Dialogue: 10,0:31:02.00,0:31:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Whale!
Dialogue: 10,0:31:06.32,0:31:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this, little one? \NYou got something to say to me? {chibikko = little kid}
Dialogue: 10,0:31:09.50,0:31:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm searching for the Water of Life. \NIf you know anything, tell me!
Dialogue: 10,0:31:13.48,0:31:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The Water of Life?
Dialogue: 10,0:31:14.48,0:31:16.09,Overlap,,0,0,0,,Yeah! You know something?
Dialogue: 10,0:31:16.09,0:31:19.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Nah, never heard of anything like that.
Dialogue: 10,0:31:19.48,0:31:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Though when it comes to seawater, \Nnobody knows more about it than me...
Dialogue: 10,0:31:25.49,0:31:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So you don't know either.
Dialogue: 10,0:31:27.17,0:31:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, the sea! I wanna go home!
Dialogue: 10,0:31:35.53,0:31:37.68,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with you, Whale?
Dialogue: 10,0:31:39.80,0:31:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,That cruel salmon tricked me!
Dialogue: 10,0:31:44.04,0:31:46.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What did the salmon do?!
Dialogue: 10,0:31:48.44,0:31:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Crying won't help me understand. \NTell me what happened!
Dialogue: 10,0:31:52.51,0:31:56.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Not like telling you will\N change anything, but...
Dialogue: 10,0:31:56.55,0:32:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I got tricked by that salmon \Nand ended up all the way here.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:01.20,0:32:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,That salmon told me there was \Nanother great sea further upriver,
Dialogue: 10,0:32:05.53,0:32:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,with wonderful scenery \Nand more shrimp than I could ever eat.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:12.73,0:32:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,So that's why you came up from the ocean?
Dialogue: 10,0:32:14.97,0:32:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,At first, the river was wide enough,
Dialogue: 10,0:32:17.60,0:32:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and watching humans scream and run \Nwhenever they saw me was pretty amusing.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:23.88,0:32:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,But then the river kept getting narrower \Nand shallower, until I couldn't move another inch.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:33.55,0:32:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna go back to the sea! \NI wanna go home!
Dialogue: 10,0:32:39.04,0:32:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:32:40.16,0:32:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta save the whale!
Dialogue: 10,0:32:41.80,0:32:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna pull him back down the river \Nuntil he can swim on his own again.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:44.95,0:32:46.88,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's dangerous.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:46.88,0:32:50.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a good chance to test whether that double strength I got from Ushi-Oni is real.
Dialogue: 10,0:32:50.31,0:32:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, watch this!
Dialogue: 10,0:32:54.56,0:32:57.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Whale, I'm gonna help you!
Dialogue: 10,0:32:58.28,0:33:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have to cry anymore!
Dialogue: 10,0:33:06.52,0:33:09.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you seriously going to...
Dialogue: 10,0:33:09.60,0:33:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey now, that's reckless!
Dialogue: 10,0:33:12.79,0:33:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou? Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:33:15.06,0:33:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Ushi-Oni! Ushi-Oni, give me twice the strength of a whale!
Dialogue: 10,0:33:26.34,0:33:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,H-Heave-ho...
Dialogue: 10,0:33:46.59,0:33:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I-I'm moving! Moving!
Dialogue: 10,0:34:09.12,0:34:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,This is incredible! {/unbelievable}
Dialogue: 10,0:34:12.79,0:34:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! We're almost there, whale! {???????? only hear "whale", could be "hey, you help too"; don't think this is in the book}
Dialogue: 10,0:34:18.43,0:34:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Th-This is...
Dialogue: 10,0:34:25.45,0:34:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa! Incredible!
Dialogue: 10,0:34:28.47,0:34:29.97,Default,,0,0,0,,My body...
Dialogue: 10,0:34:34.89,0:34:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,My body...
Dialogue: 10,0:34:50.98,0:34:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,My body...
Dialogue: 10,0:34:53.13,0:34:54.76,Default,,0,0,0,,can move. {ikuzo? let's go?}
Dialogue: 10,0:34:59.48,0:35:00.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm floating!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:07.59,0:35:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm floating!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:13.23,0:35:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm floating! Floating!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:18.67,0:35:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm floating free!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:21.92,0:35:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm floating free!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:27.34,0:35:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:30.94,0:35:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the whale?
Dialogue: 10,0:35:32.27,0:35:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:34.90,0:35:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Thanks to you, I made it! {was saved}
Dialogue: 10,0:35:40.10,0:35:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't repay you now, \Nbut if you're ever in trouble, call for me.
Dialogue: 10,0:35:46.25,0:35:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything involving the sea, I'll help with!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:49.45,0:35:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure. I'll remember that. {lit: when that time comes}
Dialogue: 10,0:35:52.32,0:35:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:55.79,0:35:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I can go back to the sea!
Dialogue: 10,0:35:58.59,0:36:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going back to the sea!
Dialogue: 10,0:36:07.70,0:36:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, there are fields! There's a village down there. Let's check it out.
Dialogue: 10,0:36:11.77,0:36:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 10,0:36:25.36,0:36:28.61,Default,,0,0,0,,There! Go, go. Good.
Dialogue: 10,0:36:34.63,0:36:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This is one weird village.
Dialogue: 10,0:36:45.07,0:36:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Even the cats are wearing weird stuff. {lit: even is even attached to a cat}
Dialogue: 10,0:36:52.98,0:36:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me...
Dialogue: 10,0:36:55.08,0:36:56.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, what is it?
Dialogue: 10,0:36:56.62,0:37:01.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, why is everybody in this village \Ncarrying boats around?
Dialogue: 10,0:37:01.74,0:37:06.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Boy, don't tell me you've never heard of the Mountain Palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:37:06.74,0:37:09.10,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this Mountain Palace?
Dialogue: 10,0:37:12.10,0:37:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Deep in these mountains, inside a palace, \Nlives a fearsome giant serpent. {orochi = giant snake; monster serpent​ - the very same as in wanpaku ouji no orochi taiji and it even does the same thing}
Dialogue: 10,0:37:16.82,0:37:19.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It causes terrible floods whenever it wants to.
Dialogue: 10,0:37:20.48,0:37:25.98,Default,,0,0,0,,So everybody here stays prepared \Nin case the floods come again.
Dialogue: 10,0:37:25.98,0:37:28.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh? And where's that Mountain Palace?
Dialogue: 10,0:37:30.13,0:37:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,That one?
Dialogue: 10,0:37:32.98,0:37:37.18,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about? \NThat's the mansion of the wealthy Awa family. {awa no chouja - not sure if awa or awano is the surname, or if it's a proper name at all bc awa means "millet" and that family is fixated on millet}
Dialogue: 10,0:37:37.18,0:37:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh? It sure looks sparkly from here.
Dialogue: 10,0:37:41.40,0:37:45.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The walls of the mansion and even\N the storehouses are coated with millet. {??? that's actually what he says, in the book: That's because they've mixed millet into the soil of the wall.}
Dialogue: 10,0:37:45.43,0:37:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 10,0:37:46.37,0:37:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And there are eighty-eight storehouses packed full of millet.
Dialogue: 10,0:37:51.27,0:37:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But two years ago, their only daughter was taken away by the master of the Mountain Palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:37:57.29,0:37:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 10,0:37:58.91,0:38:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The master and his wife grieved terribly, \Nbut there was nothing they could do.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:03.58,0:38:05.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Why doesn't anyone go rescue her?
Dialogue: 10,0:38:06.22,0:38:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the master of the Mountain Palace \Nis a terrifying monster, after all.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:10.59,0:38:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Ain't there a single brave man in this village?
Dialogue: 10,0:38:13.99,0:38:18.42,Default,,0,0,0,,There were a few,\N but not one ever came back.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:18.80,0:38:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,And besides, the wealthy Awa master \Nis greedier than any man alive. {of the millet palace, not the orochi}
Dialogue: 10,0:38:23.90,0:38:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,He won't even give a pair of straw sandals\N to someone trying to rescue the princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:28.36,0:38:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Lately, you hardly hear\N stories like that anymore,
Dialogue: 10,0:38:32.23,0:38:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,but poor Lord Awa and his wife \Nare said to cry every day.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:39.24,0:38:46.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You ought to get your boat ready too. \NYou never know when the next flood might hit.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:52.43,0:38:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you hear that, Tsubametobi?
Dialogue: 10,0:38:53.87,0:38:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I heard it.
Dialogue: 10,0:38:55.47,0:38:57.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That guy's really awful!
Dialogue: 10,0:38:57.28,0:39:00.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna go to the mountain palace \Nand defeat its master!
Dialogue: 10,0:39:00.01,0:39:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I figured you'd say that.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:03.09,0:39:07.48,Default,,0,0,0,,First, let's go to the lord's mansion. \NMaybe we'll learn something.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:08.04,0:39:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, let's.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:18.48,0:39:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Incredible. Even though the village was wrecked\N by the flood, this place is untouched.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:32.86,0:39:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been waiting for you, traveler. \NPlease, come inside.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:37.62,0:39:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Waiting for us? {\i1}Us{\i0}?
Dialogue: 10,0:39:40.78,0:39:46.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. At the lady of the house's order, \NI've been waiting since morning.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:46.39,0:39:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,She said a guest from the sky \Nwould surely come today.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:50.42,0:39:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh? How did she know?
Dialogue: 10,0:39:52.66,0:39:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, please come inside \Nand meet the lady of the house.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:56.66,0:39:58.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg of you.
Dialogue: 10,0:39:58.97,0:40:01.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Please save the princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:01.13,0:40:04.52,Default,,0,0,0,,The one who is bound to save her \Nis Maegami Tarou-dono.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:04.52,0:40:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Only you can do it and no one else.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:06.91,0:40:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard it clearly in a dream last night.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:11.55,0:40:16.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Only the one who came to our house \Nfrom the sky can save the princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:16.55,0:40:18.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, go there as soon as you can.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:18.44,0:40:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The princess is still alive, and the master...
Dialogue: 10,0:40:21.92,0:40:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The master of the palace \Nis about to make her his wife!
Dialogue: 10,0:40:27.28,0:40:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady of the house,
Dialogue: 10,0:40:28.41,0:40:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I came here because I'm planning to take down\N the master of the Mountain Palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:32.55,0:40:34.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I promise I'll save the princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:34.64,0:40:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:36.40,0:40:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much!
Dialogue: 10,0:40:44.00,0:40:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard what you said.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:45.35,0:40:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, Maegami Tarou, I don't intend to give you any reward, even if you {\i1}do{\i0} rescue the princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:51.85,0:40:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to make that abundantly clear from the start.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:55.22,0:40:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't need any reward.
Dialogue: 10,0:40:56.82,0:41:02.43,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Tarou-dono, if you wish it, \Nplease make the princess your bride.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:02.43,0:41:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That is what we've already decided. {since long ago}
Dialogue: 10,0:41:05.20,0:41:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,If you want her, she's yours. \NBut understand this.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:08.10,0:41:11.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't give you anything else: \Nno millet, no provisions, no nothing!
Dialogue: 10,0:41:12.17,0:41:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:14.17,0:41:15.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll go at once.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:15.78,0:41:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah... I almost forgot. Tarou-dono, \Nyou do have an iron sword, don't you?
Dialogue: 10,0:41:20.68,0:41:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't have anything like that. \NBut I've got Tsubametobi, so I'm fine.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:25.38,0:41:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That won't do!
Dialogue: 10,0:41:27.22,0:41:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard a revelation
Dialogue: 10,0:41:29.06,0:41:33.23,Default,,0,0,0,,that if you don't have an iron sword, \Nthe master of the palace will kill you.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:34.70,0:41:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 10,0:41:37.16,0:41:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a problem. \NWhere on Earth could I find an iron sword?
Dialogue: 10,0:41:40.74,0:41:42.64,Default,,0,0,0,,In the Dragon Palace. {from urashima taro's fairy tale: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ry%C5%ABg%C5%AB-j%C5%8D}
Dialogue: 10,0:41:42.64,0:41:44.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The Dragon Palace?
Dialogue: 10,0:41:44.04,0:41:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, it's been said since ages past that\N there's an iron sword is in the Dragon Palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:41:50.91,0:41:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir! Sir! The Mountain Palace is coming into view!
Dialogue: 10,0:41:55.38,0:41:56.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 10,0:41:56.85,0:42:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, there it is. \NThere! That's the Mountain Palace!
Dialogue: 10,0:42:09.16,0:42:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What a creepy palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:42:11.17,0:42:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,A few times a year, the clouds part \Nand you can see it,
Dialogue: 10,0:42:14.80,0:42:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,but then the clouds quickly rise again and...
Dialogue: 10,0:42:17.84,0:42:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, see? It's disappearing already.
Dialogue: 10,0:42:21.84,0:42:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It's disappearing... Disappearing!
Dialogue: 10,0:42:24.90,0:42:30.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Princess... Princess! \NWe've finally found someone to save you!
Dialogue: 10,0:42:30.52,0:42:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't lose heart!
Dialogue: 10,0:42:33.39,0:42:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It's disappearing...
Dialogue: 10,0:42:36.12,0:42:38.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Princess! Princess...
Dialogue: 10,0:42:39.69,0:42:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady of the house! {proprietress/mistress}
Dialogue: 10,0:42:41.16,0:42:43.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady of the house, please stay strong!
Dialogue: 10,0:42:43.77,0:42:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady of the house!
Dialogue: 10,0:42:49.19,0:42:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, do you know where that Dragon Palace is?
Dialogue: 10,0:42:52.04,0:42:54.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I only know it's somewhere under the sea.
Dialogue: 10,0:42:54.84,0:42:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,The sea is vast enough to swallow the sun \Nand endless beyond measure.
Dialogue: 10,0:43:00.75,0:43:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it! Let's ask the whale. \NMaybe he knows something.
Dialogue: 10,0:43:37.25,0:43:40.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder if my voice can reach him in this huge sea.
Dialogue: 10,0:43:43.39,0:43:52.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Whale!
Dialogue: 10,0:43:53.63,0:44:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come out! It's Maegami Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:44:05.71,0:44:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Try calling again.
Dialogue: 10,0:44:10.12,0:44:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Whale!
Dialogue: 10,0:44:18.36,0:44:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Come out, please! It's Maegami Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:44:32.39,0:44:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Maegami Tarou! \NDid you call me? {/do you need something from me}
Dialogue: 10,0:44:42.55,0:44:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the whale!
Dialogue: 10,0:44:55.68,0:44:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We're almost at the entrance\N to the Dragon Palace,
Dialogue: 10,0:44:58.83,0:45:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,so hold your breath as long as you can \Nand close your eyes!
Dialogue: 10,0:45:02.18,0:45:03.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Are we supposed to go underwater? {into the sea}
Dialogue: 10,0:45:03.97,0:45:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 10,0:45:04.84,0:45:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Do I just hold my breath?
Dialogue: 10,0:45:06.84,0:45:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as you can.
Dialogue: 10,0:45:08.21,0:45:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 10,0:45:08.86,0:45:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a deep breath.
Dialogue: 10,0:45:41.54,0:45:42.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't do it anymore!
Dialogue: 10,0:45:42.84,0:45:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,
Dialogue: 10,0:45:44.64,0:45:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou, you can breathe now.
Dialogue: 10,0:45:49.48,0:45:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, that's the Dragon Palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:45:52.34,0:45:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow...
Dialogue: 10,0:46:57.23,0:46:57.97,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no!
Dialogue: 10,0:46:57.97,0:47:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't do that, \Nespecially to a dear guest of ours.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:02.62,0:47:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Say, Princess, who is that person? {https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oto-hime}
Dialogue: 10,0:47:05.91,0:47:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Who?
Dialogue: 10,0:47:06.46,0:47:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That man came all the way here\N to get this sword so he can defeat
Dialogue: 10,0:47:09.33,0:47:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,the great serpent who caused trouble\N here in the Dragon Palace and ran away.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:13.23,0:47:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, let me pass.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:18.34,0:47:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, this is the iron sword.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:20.61,0:47:23.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:23.28,0:47:26.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, Tarou, something is worrying me.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:26.78,0:47:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry. With this, \NI can handle that giant serpent easily.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:30.67,0:47:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The thing is, when that giant serpent \Nfled the Dragon Palace,
Dialogue: 10,0:47:34.69,0:47:37.78,Default,,0,0,0,,he stole a golden pitcher\N containing the Water of Life.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:37.78,0:47:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? The Water of Life?
Dialogue: 10,0:47:40.29,0:47:44.18,Default,,0,0,0,,If the water in that pitcher is sprinkled\N on the dead, it returns them to life.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:44.18,0:47:45.68,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what worries me.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:45.68,0:47:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. So the Water of Life I was searching for \Nwas in the Mountain Palace all along?
Dialogue: 10,0:47:51.81,0:47:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 10,0:47:53.01,0:47:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Do your best.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:54.94,0:47:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I will.
Dialogue: 10,0:47:57.71,0:48:03.97,Default,,0,0,0,,If I defeat that giant serpent, I'll save the Awa lord's princess, the villagers, and the Firebird too.
Dialogue: 10,0:48:04.62,0:48:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And if the Firebird can fly again from Doudou Mountain...
Dialogue: 10,0:48:08.81,0:48:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,then everyone in my village will be happy too.
Dialogue: 10,0:48:20.72,0:48:25.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, Princess{oto-hime I assume, not the one in captivity}, lend me your strength \Nas I enter the Mountain Palace! {lit: aiming for the mountain palace}
Dialogue: 10,0:48:33.98,0:48:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady of the house! \NLady of the house!
Dialogue: 10,0:48:36.55,0:48:39.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Maegami Tarou has come back!
Dialogue: 10,0:48:41.26,0:48:43.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! He's done it!
Dialogue: 10,0:48:43.59,0:48:49.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah... Tarou-dono! Tarou-dono! \NWe're counting on you!
Dialogue: 10,0:48:47.70,0:48:55.42,Song,,0,0,0,,I'm Maegami Tarou from Kazefukan Village {same song as before; 僕 僕 風ふかん村の\Nまえがみ太郎さ\N\N天 ゆるがす\Nいなずまさえも\N\N地 ひきさく\N大雨さえも\N\Nへいちゃら\Nへいちゃら\Nしゃんしゃか\Nしゃんしゃか\Nびゅびゅーん\Nびゅびゅーん\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\N太郎のつるぎで お姫様\Nソレ 助け出せ 助け出せ\N\Nしゃんしゃか\Nひゅんひゅら\Nびゅびゅーん\N\N御殿の大蛇は悪者じゃ\Nヤァー きりかかれ\Nきりかかれ\N\N僕 僕 風ふかん村の\Nまえがみ太郎さ\N\N天 ゆるがす\Nいなずまさえも\N\N地 ひきさく\N大雨さえも\N\Nへいちゃら\Nへいちゃら\N}
Dialogue: 10,0:48:55.42,0:48:59.37,Song,,0,0,0,,Even thunder that shakes the heavens
Dialogue: 10,0:48:59.37,0:49:03.44,Song,,0,0,0,,Even rain that splits the earth apart
Dialogue: 10,0:49:03.44,0:49:07.68,Song,,0,0,0,,Doesn't scare me!
Dialogue: 10,0:49:07.68,0:49:11.32,Song,,0,0,0,,Shanshaka hyun-hyura byu-byuun
Dialogue: 10,0:49:11.32,0:49:23.28,Song,,0,0,0,,With Tarou's sword, the princess there! \NSave her, save her!
Dialogue: 10,0:49:23.28,0:49:26.87,Song,,0,0,0,,Shanshaka hyun-hyura byu-byuun
Dialogue: 10,0:49:26.87,0:49:30.27,Song,,0,0,0,,The great serpent in the palace is a villain
Dialogue: 10,0:49:30.27,0:49:38.48,Song,,0,0,0,,Yeah! Cut him down! Cut him down!
Dialogue: 10,0:49:38.48,0:49:46.12,Song,,0,0,0,,I'm Maegami Tarou from Kazefukan Village
Dialogue: 10,0:49:46.12,0:49:50.09,Song,,0,0,0,,Even thunder that shakes the heavens
Dialogue: 10,0:49:50.09,0:49:54.16,Song,,0,0,0,,Even rain that splits the earth apart
Dialogue: 10,0:49:54.16,0:49:59.20,Song,,0,0,0,,Doesn't scare me!
Dialogue: 10,0:49:01.78,0:49:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that the Mountain Palace?
Dialogue: 10,0:49:03.44,0:49:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 10,0:49:04.38,0:49:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like it's covered with fire.
Dialogue: 10,0:49:06.82,0:49:09.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, how do we get close to it?
Dialogue: 10,0:49:09.92,0:49:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,First, we have to put out the fire. \NI'll call the rain. Hold on tight.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:02.47,0:50:06.01,Default,,0,0,0,,What a strange palace. \NWhere's the entrance?
Dialogue: 10,0:50:08.21,0:50:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, there's a beautiful horse!
Dialogue: 10,0:50:13.51,0:50:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Princess! Are you Lord Awa's princess?
Dialogue: 10,0:50:19.82,0:50:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 10,0:50:21.86,0:50:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Maegami Tarou. \NI've come to save the princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:25.76,0:50:27.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Please show me the way in.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:27.76,0:50:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the giant serpent's palace. \NThere's no entrance for humans.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:32.53,0:50:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, there has to be at least\N one door somewhere,
Dialogue: 10,0:50:37.67,0:50:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,but humans wouldn't be able to move it.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:41.71,0:50:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It must weigh ten or twenty times \Nas much as you do.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:45.08,0:50:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I got it! \NI'm coming over there now!
Dialogue: 10,0:50:52.75,0:50:54.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou! Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:50:54.59,0:50:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it, Tsubametobi?
Dialogue: 10,0:50:56.02,0:50:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It's here, the place with the door.
Dialogue: 10,0:50:58.49,0:50:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,All right!
Dialogue: 10,0:51:02.86,0:51:05.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Ushi-Oni! Ushi-Oni!
Dialogue: 10,0:51:05.66,0:51:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Maegami Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:51:07.37,0:51:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me twice the strength of this rock!
Dialogue: 10,0:51:32.59,0:51:33.36,Default,,0,0,0,,There!
Dialogue: 10,0:51:40.00,0:51:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Maegami Tarou, you're strong!
Dialogue: 10,0:51:42.54,0:51:44.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Sit tight! I'm coming!
Dialogue: 10,0:52:24.72,0:52:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm so glad you're alive, Princess.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:27.08,0:52:28.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:28.68,0:52:30.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What should I do?
Dialogue: 10,0:52:30.49,0:52:34.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The giant serpent came up from the bottom of the swamp to make me his bride.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:35.61,0:52:43.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I've put him off with excuses until today, \Nbut at last, this is the day of the wedding.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:44.77,0:52:47.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Princess, you have me now.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:47.33,0:52:48.90,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no need to cry.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:48.90,0:52:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, take me to your wedding chamber.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:52.34,0:52:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,More important, let's escape \Nbefore the giant serpent gets here.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:55.71,0:52:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to defeat that snake no matter what.
Dialogue: 10,0:52:59.28,0:53:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, where's the bridal chamber?
Dialogue: 10,0:53:01.48,0:53:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 10,0:53:02.28,0:53:05.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right, Princess. I have a good idea.
Dialogue: 10,0:53:05.52,0:53:06.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen...
Dialogue: 10,0:54:10.88,0:54:14.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, so you've already changed \Ninto your bridal gown?
Dialogue: 10,0:54:18.54,0:54:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Since you were so beautiful picking flowers, \NI brought you back with me before I knew it.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:23.30,0:54:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You've grown up nicely.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:25.73,0:54:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then, let's exchange wedding cups. {japanese nuptial cups ritual}
Dialogue: 10,0:54:28.47,0:54:29.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:29.15,0:54:34.97,Default,,0,0,0,,From today on, you'll become my bride \Nand live with me in this swamp palace.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:34.97,0:54:36.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What a wonderful occasion.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:38.31,0:54:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, it certainly is.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:39.90,0:54:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong? Have you caught a cold?\N Your voice sounds strange.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:44.25,0:54:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, well... since it's such\N a wonderful wedding day,
Dialogue: 10,0:54:48.59,0:54:52.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought I'd take a little Water of Life \Nand get better quickly.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:53.13,0:54:54.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The Water of Life?
Dialogue: 10,0:54:55.40,0:54:57.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well. I'll think it over.
Dialogue: 10,0:54:57.20,0:54:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, pour my sake.
Dialogue: 10,0:55:06.74,0:55:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?!
Dialogue: 10,0:55:15.28,0:55:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Maegami Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,0:55:17.05,0:55:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I came to take back the Water of Life \Nyou stole from the Dragon Palace!
Dialogue: 10,0:55:24.39,0:55:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Fool! So you've come all this way \Njust to throw your life away, huh?
Dialogue: 10,0:55:32.13,0:55:34.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take your life!
Dialogue: 10,0:55:36.09,0:55:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,In a moment, you'll be stuffed into my belly.
Dialogue: 10,0:56:10.17,0:56:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Ushi-Oni! Ushi-Oni! Give me strength! \NTwice his strength!
Dialogue: 10,0:56:16.88,0:56:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah! Crap...
Dialogue: 10,0:56:37.88,0:56:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi!
Dialogue: 10,0:56:41.62,0:56:44.24,Default,,0,0,0,,This sword simply bounces off his head.
Dialogue: 10,0:56:44.24,0:56:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou, it's his neck. Aim for his neck!
Dialogue: 10,0:56:47.31,0:56:50.28,Default,,0,0,0,,And hurry! The flood hit the village!
Dialogue: 10,0:56:50.28,0:56:51.51,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, got it!
Dialogue: 10,0:57:02.69,0:57:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I got him!
Dialogue: 10,0:57:14.30,0:57:15.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 10,0:57:23.58,0:57:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Take this!
Dialogue: 10,0:57:52.62,0:57:56.18,Default,,0,0,0,,My storehouses are floating away!\N My storehouses! {/being washed away}
Dialogue: 10,0:57:56.18,0:58:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Nobody touch it!\N These storehouses are mine!{false i-frame}
Dialogue: 10,0:58:00.52,0:58:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter where they go,\N they're my storehouses!
Dialogue: 10,0:58:05.89,0:58:09.16,Default,,0,0,0,,These storehouses are mine. \NThey belong to me.
Dialogue: 10,0:58:09.16,0:58:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter where they go, \Nthey're my storehouses!
Dialogue: 10,0:58:21.15,0:58:24.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, why are you running away?\N Are you tired?
Dialogue: 10,0:58:24.05,0:58:26.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave it to me.
Dialogue: 10,0:58:26.14,0:58:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's coming!
Dialogue: 10,0:58:33.38,0:58:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now! Hurry, get the pitcher!
Dialogue: 10,0:58:40.36,0:58:41.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The Water of Life!
Dialogue: 10,0:58:49.00,0:58:52.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Ushi-Oni! Ushi-Oni!\N Give me double strength!
Dialogue: 10,0:58:52.53,0:58:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Double his strength! {doesn't say "his" but I assume that's what he means}
Dialogue: 10,0:59:50.49,0:59:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That flood was terrible.
Dialogue: 10,0:59:54.83,0:59:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, it's the lady of the house.
Dialogue: 10,1:00:02.04,1:00:03.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 10,1:00:03.70,1:00:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Princess! Princess, is that you?
Dialogue: 10,1:00:07.02,1:00:08.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 10,1:00:08.14,1:00:11.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Princess! You've returned. \NYou've really returned!
Dialogue: 10,1:00:11.95,1:00:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother...
Dialogue: 10,1:00:28.23,1:00:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Is Doudou Mountain much further? {are we there yet}
Dialogue: 10,1:00:30.17,1:00:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure.\NAh! There it is, Doudou Mountain.
Dialogue: 10,1:00:35.54,1:00:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, the Firebird's waiting.
Dialogue: 10,1:00:38.18,1:00:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Tsubametobi, put us down \Nin front of the Firebird's cave.
Dialogue: 10,1:00:50.75,1:00:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Firebird!
Dialogue: 10,1:00:52.57,1:00:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you here, Firebird?
Dialogue: 10,1:00:55.51,1:01:00.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It's me! Maegami Tarou! \NI've brought you the Water of Life!
Dialogue: 10,1:01:01.54,1:01:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Tarou? And the Water of Life?
Dialogue: 10,1:01:05.08,1:01:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,With this, you'll be able to fly again.
Dialogue: 10,1:01:08.10,1:01:11.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard about it from the New Year's Spirit, \Nso I found it for you.
Dialogue: 10,1:01:11.54,1:01:15.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I see, so that was it? \NI was already beginning to give up.
Dialogue: 10,1:01:17.28,1:01:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on, pour it over me. Splash it all over.
Dialogue: 10,1:01:21.55,1:01:23.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Here goes, Firebird.
Dialogue: 10,1:01:43.74,1:01:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The strength is flowing back into me!
Dialogue: 10,1:01:55.98,1:01:58.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't fly yet. \NI need more of that water.
Dialogue: 10,1:01:58.99,1:02:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,There isn't a drop left.
Dialogue: 10,1:02:01.11,1:02:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why did you bring the Water of Life? \NOnly to mock me? {tease/make fun of}
Dialogue: 10,1:02:05.09,1:02:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Try it one more time, Firebird!
Dialogue: 10,1:02:10.57,1:02:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No good. I can't fly. \NMy legs... My legs won't move.
Dialogue: 10,1:02:15.10,1:02:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, I'll go down and\N try to move them for you!
Dialogue: 10,1:02:27.75,1:02:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Ushi-Oni! Ushi-Oni! \NGive me double strength! Double strength!
Dialogue: 10,1:02:33.62,1:02:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it...
Dialogue: 10,1:02:35.62,1:02:39.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Impossible! How come his legs\N won't even budge?! {lit: to think something like this won't move}
Dialogue: 10,1:02:42.80,1:02:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,1:02:44.03,1:02:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Tarou, have you forgotten \Nwhat the New Year's Spirit told you?
Dialogue: 10,1:02:48.40,1:02:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,H-Huh? What was it again?
Dialogue: 10,1:02:50.35,1:02:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The Water of Life alone won't be enough\N to make the Firebird fly.
Dialogue: 10,1:02:54.27,1:02:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, right! I forgot.
Dialogue: 10,1:02:59.28,1:03:01.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Firebird!
Dialogue: 10,1:03:01.01,1:03:05.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The New Year's Spirit said there was\N something you had to cast away!
Dialogue: 10,1:03:05.32,1:03:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do, you'll be able to fly\N through the sky again!
Dialogue: 10,1:03:07.82,1:03:09.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know what it is?
Dialogue: 10,1:03:09.39,1:03:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Something to cast away?
Dialogue: 10,1:03:11.06,1:03:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. Something to cast away.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:16.80,1:03:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Beneath my feet lies a great deal \Nof gold hidden away.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:21.45,1:03:24.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I love shiny things.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:24.36,1:03:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,When I found that gold, I decided it was mine, \Nand I'd never give it to anyone.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:29.29,1:03:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What? So you've just been guarding gold?
Dialogue: 10,1:03:31.88,1:03:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:33.61,1:03:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,And before you knew it, \Nyour body stopped moving too?
Dialogue: 10,1:03:37.65,1:03:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't do it. I can't cast away my gold!
Dialogue: 10,1:03:41.42,1:03:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 10,1:03:43.69,1:03:46.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You should just cast it away.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:46.09,1:03:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Being able to soar freely through the skies \Nis way, way better than gold!
Dialogue: 10,1:03:55.87,1:03:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Firebird, maybe it's not that you can't fly.
Dialogue: 10,1:03:58.97,1:04:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe the truth is you don't want to fly? \NAnd you have to decide which it is.
Dialogue: 10,1:04:10.38,1:04:13.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye, Firebird!
Dialogue: 10,1:04:17.66,1:04:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Princess. \NOne more flight and we'll be home.
Dialogue: 10,1:05:00.90,1:05:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! It's the Firebird! \NIt flew away from Doudou Mountain!
Dialogue: 10,1:05:15.38,1:05:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The Firebird chose the sky. {tobu hou? being able to fly?}
Dialogue: 10,1:05:35.24,1:05:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! Look there! \NDoudou Mountain is collapsing!
Dialogue: 10,1:06:12.89,1:06:16.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, the sunlight's pouring through! \NIt's the light of the sun! {??? idk what he's talking about}
Dialogue: 10,1:06:16.64,1:06:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Happiness is coming to this village too!
Dialogue: 10,1:06:19.02,1:06:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. And there was gold\N hidden inside Doudou Mountain too.
Dialogue: 10,1:06:22.56,1:06:24.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The bird left it behind.
Dialogue: 10,1:06:24.87,1:06:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, isn't that Tarou?
Dialogue: 10,1:06:27.29,1:06:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That's Maegami Tarou, ain't it?
Dialogue: 10,1:06:29.96,1:06:33.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa! Grandma!
Dialogue: 10,1:06:46.01,1:06:48.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa! Grandma!
Dialogue: 10,1:06:49.18,1:06:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Th-That's Tarou's voice. No mistaking it. \NThis isn't a dream, is it?
Dialogue: 10,1:06:54.28,1:06:55.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed!
Dialogue: 10,1:07:02.22,1:07:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,1:07:04.09,1:07:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It really is our Tarou!
Dialogue: 10,1:07:07.56,1:07:13.33,Narrator,,0,0,0,,After that, Tarou and the princess happily held their wedding ceremony.
Dialogue: 10,1:07:14.60,1:07:20.14,Narrator,,0,0,0,,And after Doudou Mountain collapsed, \Nfresh winds blew through the village. {remember that village is called kazefukan = windless}
Dialogue: 10,1:07:20.14,1:07:26.25,Narrator,,0,0,0,,The crops flourished, gold was found,\N and everyone prospered and lived happily.
Dialogue: 10,1:07:24.25,1:07:29.16,Song,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow is New Year's Day
Dialogue: 10,1:07:29.16,1:07:34.39,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing {same song as before}
Dialogue: 10,1:07:34.39,1:07:39.44,Song,,0,0,0,,Eating mochi whiter than snow
Dialogue: 10,1:07:39.44,1:07:44.53,Song,,0,0,0,,And drinking sake smooth as oil
Dialogue: 10,1:07:44.53,1:07:50.34,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing
Dialogue: 10,1:07:50.97,1:07:56.04,Song,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, tomorrow is New Year's day
Dialogue: 10,1:07:56.04,1:08:01.08,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing
Dialogue: 10,1:08:01.08,1:08:06.02,Song,,0,0,0,,Eating mochi whiter than snow
Dialogue: 10,1:08:06.02,1:08:10.57,Song,,0,0,0,,And drinking sake smooth as oil
Dialogue: 10,1:08:10.57,1:08:17.40,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing
Dialogue: 10,1:08:17.40,1:08:22.34,Song,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, tomorrow is New Year's Day
Dialogue: 10,1:08:22.34,1:08:27.31,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing
Dialogue: 10,1:08:24.44,1:08:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,New Year's Spirit! Thank you!
Dialogue: 10,1:08:27.31,1:08:32.18,Song,,0,0,0,,Eating mochi whiter than snow
Dialogue: 10,1:08:32.18,1:08:37.08,Song,,0,0,0,,And drinking sake smooth as oil
Dialogue: 10,1:08:37.08,1:08:42.49,Song,,0,0,0,,New Year's is a wonderful thing
